# Deploy

When the user says **deploy**, **ship**, or **publish** (to prod):

1. Run `git status` only.
2. If the working tree has notable undocumented user-facing changes, update docs/changelog first (see `maintain-project-docs` skill), then continue.
3. Confirm Wrangler auth (one short check):

```bash
export PATH="$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.18.0/bin:$PATH"
cd rtikhonov.com
NODE_OPTIONS="--dns-result-order=ipv4first" npx wrangler whoami
```

Accept either a logged-in **OAuth** session or `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` (+ optional `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`). Do not start a long API-token tutorial if `whoami` already shows this account.

4. Deploy:

```bash
export PATH="$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.18.0/bin:$PATH"
cd rtikhonov.com && npm run deploy
```

Use network permissions. Expect ~30–60s. `npm run deploy` already runs `check:docs` and the build.

5. Spot-check live with the `check-live-site` skill (`curl` + flag expectations). Reply with live URLs and the Wrangler Version ID.

Live: `https://rtikhonov.com`, `https://www.rtikhonov.com`, `https://rtikhonov.inrome.workers.dev`.

## Auth blocked

If `whoami` fails and there is no token:

- Prefer Cursor environment secret `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` (Edit Cloudflare Workers template).
- Optional: `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`.
- Do not paste tokens into chat or the repo.
- After the user adds a secret, check env / `whoami` again — secrets may only appear on a **new** agent run.

## Do not

- TodoWrite for deploy
- `git diff main...HEAD` (or large branch diffs) unless the deploy failed
- Manual README / `docs/` / CHANGELOG review when `git status` is clean
- Separate `check:docs` or `astro build` before `npm run deploy`
- Commit or push unless the user asks
- Assume GitHub Actions or Pages ships this site

Agent shells often lack Node on PATH. Always export the nvm path above (or `source ~/.nvm/nvm.sh && nvm use`) before npm/astro/wrangler.
